    "body": "@annevk that proposal has gazillion comments, and I actually stopped understanding it at the second `let textToken = changes.firstChild(token);` line, as it's not clear where that `token` comes from, but if it's able to apply many changes at once in an optimized way, including inner DOM nodes manipulation, then it seems to address already this proposal too, so I believe we might close this one, and hope that one will end up working for the scenario mentioned in here too.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?",
